    "featuredAlt": "ice cream beans from Big Island arent just delicious ",
    "text": "Hi hi!! It’s me—Ipo 💖\nLet’s talk about one of the quiet heroes in Fruity Puppy… the soft, silky, cloud-like fruit that doesn’t scream for attention—but absolutely earns its place:\n\n👉 Ice Cream Bean (yes, it’s real… and yes, it’s magical)\n\n🌿 The Gentle Protector\n\nIce cream bean (Inga edulis) is like the guardian spirit of your skin. While some ingredients come in hot—exfoliating, brightening, activating—ice cream bean does something just as important: it protects, cushions, and conditions.\n\nIts pulp is naturally rich in polysaccharides—long-chain sugars that bind water and create a soft, breathable film—along with amino compounds that help reinforce skin structure and natural humectants that pull moisture into the skin and keep it there. Translation? It forms a hydration shield that keeps your skin plump, calm, and resilient.\n\n⚖️ The Synergy: Teamwork Makes the Glow Work\n\nNow here’s where Fruity Puppy gets next-level. Ice cream bean doesn’t work alone—it works in harmony with the rest of the formula.\n\nLilikoi (passionfruit) is packed with vitamin C and gentle fruit acids that brighten, refine, and softly resurface the skin. Papaya brings papain enzymes that break down dead skin and clear the way for fresh, healthy cells. Spearmint steps in with cooling, antibacterial, circulation-boosting properties that wake up the skin and calm inflammation.\n\n🧠 So What’s Actually Happing?\n\nThink of it like this:\n\nLilikoi, papaya, and mint are the workers—they exfoliate, renew, stimulate, and do the heavy lifting. Ice cream bean is the protector—it makes sure your skin stays hydrated, calm, and intact while all that work is happening.\n\nWithout that protection, active ingredients can sometimes leave skin dry, irritated, or vulnerable. With ice cream bean, the work happens without damage, the skin stays soft and supported, and the results go deeper and last longer.\n\n🧬 The Fruity Puppy Difference\n\nThis is where your formula stands apart. You’re not just mixing ingredients—you’re building a balanced system.\n\nActive fruits transform the skin. Botanical intelligence guides the process. Structural support—ice cream bean paired with your complex fat lattice—delivers and protects.\n\nIt’s not about stripping the skin and hoping for the best. It’s about renewing the skin while protecting its integrity at every step.\n\n💖 Final Thought from Ipo\n\nIf lilikoi and papaya are doing the work, then ice cream bean is the one saying: “Don’t worry—I’ve got you. You’re safe while we grow.”\n\nThat’s why your skin doesn’t just look better—it feels better, heals better, and stays stronger over time."
