    "featuredAlt": "Ipo the fruity puppy loves the farmers market the most because she loves the other vendors on big island",
    "text": "The Complete Guide to Fruity Puppy Skincare (Antioxidants from Big Island)\n\naloha,\n\nI’m Ipo, the antioxidant-obsessed pink puppy here to walk you through everything magical and practical about Fruity Puppy—the natural tropical fruit skincare cream handcrafted on the Big Island of Hawai‘i. Whether you’re sunburned, tattooed, or just tired of dry skin, this thick little jar is about to become your best friend. Let’s dive in.\n\nWhy We Made Fruity Puppy\n\nJessie, the man at the farmers market (and the farmer-inventor behind Fruity Puppy), made this cream for real island life: cracked knuckles, sun-toasted shoulders, healing tattoos, and skin that needs antioxidant love. Everything is grown on volcanic soil and perfected with care. Fruity Puppy is thick on purpose, rich in tropical antioxidants, and made with rare botanicals like lilikoi, papaya, cranberry hibiscus, and spearmint.\n\nThe Problem: Skin Under Stress\n\nThe sun, salt, wind, and daily life put real stress on your skin. If you’ve got dryness, irritation, or slow healing, you’re not alone. Most lotions don’t cut it—they evaporate fast or use fillers like petroleum. You need nutrients. You need antioxidants.\n\nWhy Antioxidants Matter\n\nWhen your skin is exposed to UV rays, pollution, or micro-damage, it creates oxidative stress. That’s when free radicals mess with your skin cells and healing slows down. Antioxidants help neutralize those free radicals and support your skin’s recovery. Fruity Puppy is packed with tropical antioxidants from plants grown in volcanic soil—real power from real fruit.\n\nWhat’s Inside Fruity Puppy (And Why It Works)\n\nWe use 11 ingredients. That’s it. No fluff, no fillers.\n\nTropical fruit and plant power:\n\nLilikoi (passionfruit): brightens and defends against sun damage\n\nPapaya: softens and gently smooths with natural enzymes\n\nCranberry hibiscus: soothes inflammation with rich antioxidants\n\nSpearmint: clarifies and refreshes\n\nAloe vera: hydrates and cools\n\nButters and oils:\n\nMango butter: rich, creamy, seals in moisture\n\nShea butter: softens and supports elasticity\n\nDeodorized cocoa butter: smooth and scent-neutral\n\nCoconut oil: locks in hydration\n\nSkin-protecting extras:\n\nVitamin E: helps healing and reduces scarring\n\nAloe vera gel: adds another layer of hydration\n\nThis blend makes Fruity Puppy one of the best antioxidant creams for sensitive skin.\n\nHow to Use Fruity Puppy\n\nIt’s thicker than a lotion, richer than a balm, and designed to stay put.\n\nDaily use:\n\nScoop a pea-size dab\n\nMelt it between your fingers\n\nMassage onto dry, burned, or stressed skin\n\nFor sunburns:\n\nCool your skin first\n\nApply a thin layer of cream\n\nLet it absorb gently\n\nFor tattoos:\n\nDab onto clean, dry skin\n\nReapply 2–3 times daily\n\nHelps with healing and color vibrancy\n\nFor cracked hands or heels:\n\nApply generously before bed\n\nCover with socks or gloves to lock in moisture\n\nGrease cleanup:\nOne day, Ryan used Fruity Puppy after working on his car—the butters cut the grease in seconds. We filmed it, laughed, and went right back to our antioxidant routine.\n\nWhy It’s Thick on Purpose\n\nPeople ask why Fruity Puppy isn’t whipped or light. Because that’s not the point. It’s thick so it stays where you put it and lasts a long time. A little goes a very long way.\n\nIngredient Spotlight\n\nPapaya: softens and gently exfoliates\n\nCranberry hibiscus: calms redness with antioxidants\n\nLilikoi: supports bright, sun-stressed skin with vitamin C\n\nWhere It’s Made\n\nEvery jar of Fruity Puppy starts on the Big Island of Hawai‘i, where Jessie grows the ingredients himself. It’s small-batch, farm-to-jar skincare made without shortcuts.\n\nFAQ\n\nIs Fruity Puppy safe for sensitive skin?\nYes. It’s a gentle antioxidant skin cream with hibiscus, aloe, and vitamin E.\n\nHow much should I use?\nA pea-size dab. It’s thick on purpose and melts in as you massage.\n\nCan I use it on sunburns?\nYes. Apply a thin layer after cooling the skin. Antioxidants and aloe support recovery.\n\nIs it good for tattoos?\nYes. It hydrates and protects new ink while supporting color vibrancy.\n\nWhere is it made?\nOn the Big Island of Hawai‘i, using tropical, farm-grown ingredients.\n\n\n\nYour skin deserves the same care and curiosity we bring to every jar. Whether you're sun-kissed, freshly inked, or just need a little daily repair, Fruity Puppy is here to help you feel good in your skin—with tropical antioxidants, volcanic richness, and a touch of robot-puppy love.\n\nWith love from Big Island — Ipo 🐾"
